# doomcode formatting on Put: ~/.config/doomcode/fmt
#
# The uncommented lines are the built-in defaults. Each rule is a file
# suffix (with the dot) or an exact file name, then a command that reads
# the text on stdin and prints it formatted; %f is the file's path.
# "name -" removes a rule; "put off" stops formatting on Put (Fmt still
# works). "Fmt rules" shows the rules; after a change: Fmt reload.

.go      gofmt
put      on

# More formatters, if you have them installed:
# .rs    rustfmt --emit stdout
# .py    black -q -
# .ts    prettier --stdin-filepath %f
# .json  jq .
